# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NYXEN PORTFOLIO — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in what you need.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
# Both variables here are optional, and neither is a browser secret: only
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values reach the client, and GITHUB_TOKEN is server-only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── GitHub ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL. The site works without this: public repository data is fetched
# unauthenticated (60 requests/hour/IP, which ISR keeps you well under).
#
# Add a token to raise the limit to 5,000 requests/hour, which matters only if
# you rebuild frequently.
#
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta
# A fine-grained token with NO account permissions and read-only public access
# is enough. Do not grant repo write scopes.
GITHUB_TOKEN=


# ── Site URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL. Overrides siteConfig.url for absolute metadata URLs.
# On Vercel this is inferred automatically; set it only for custom setups.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
